SBA 316: 
The Document Object Model

NBA Score‑Keeper” click‑counter game

Concept – User selects a team from a dropdown, enters a target score, 
then clicks a “+1” button to simulate scoring. The app updates the displayed score, 
validates that the input is a positive integer, and stops when the target is reached.

Single‑page HTML – one index.html

Form/input validation – <input type="number" min="1" required> for target score; 

DOM caching – cache dropdown, input, score display, button, message element.

Event listeners – submit on the form (to set target), click on the “+1” button.